 They have daily specials that always sound good too. Allegro is a great meet up spot for drinks after work if you work in the CBD or like I mentioned, on game days. Go Saints!"},{"business_id":"WVC_vAgf8EEwOGpWUT4WGQ","review_id":"BKMz18j0QFrTUaR0rm7nxQ","date":"2011-09-07T13:50:36","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9165542125701904,"text_excerpt":"I think if Allegro's was located anywhere else in the city it wouldn't be what it is but... location location location! They do serve up a good pre game Bloody Mary on Saints gamedays. The food inside is ok and the decor reminds me of the 80's (including their sign). Service is good for mid day lunch and drinks except for on gamedays, this place gets PACKED. It's one of the best places to get together in the CBD, everyone knows it."},{"business_id":"WVC_vAgf8EEwOGpWUT4WGQ","review_id":"sqHtO-D8CWa-xMxy-w5GOw","date":"2010-11-06T15:44:03","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.8971139192581177,"text_excerpt":"Eat your fingers good! As long as I have worked in the CBD, this was my first time here. What has taken me so long? This place is a hidden gem. I had the barbecue shrimp plate which was served with a choice of side. I had the fries and crusty french bread. A-maz-ing! I was mad it was gone. An added bonus was that the shrimp were deveined!"}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
